<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Boot's console logging, with one change: the password of a URL (scheme://user:password@host) is
masked on every line, message and stack trace alike.

Why: WebClient writes the full request URL, userinfo included, into the message of an error answer
("401 Unauthorized from GET http://user:password@host/...") and into the "Request to GET ..."
checkpoint of its stack trace. With the cause now kept on TechnicalException, those traces reach the
ERROR log. No URL here is meant to carry credentials (callers' secrets travel in a header, Garage's
keys sign the query, which WebClient leaves out of its messages, and the signer rebuilds every
request URL from scheme, host and port only), so this is a safety net for a mistyped
MEDIA_INTERNAL_ENDPOINT or MEDIA_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT, not a feature.

The whole Boot pattern is wrapped in %replace, then %nopex stops logback from appending a second,
unmasked stack trace of its own.
-->
<configuration>
	<include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/defaults.xml"/>

	<property name="CONSOLE_LOG_PATTERN"
			  value="%replace(${CONSOLE_LOG_PATTERN}){'(://[^/\s:@]+:)[^/\s@]+@', '$1****@'}%nopex"/>

	<include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/console-appender.xml"/>

	<root level="INFO">
		<appender-ref ref="CONSOLE"/>
	</root>
</configuration>
